            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Nuclear spent fuel reprocessing plant</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="0c26eb8b-39fd-3bfd-84f1-c7bdd4b269c0">waste</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="d7ff4edc-64a9-336e-bb1d-3c3744dd4513">nuclear waste</common:class>
                    <common:class level="2" classId="45dff45c-3350-3654-901d-56a70ac193f7">infrastructure</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">Data on material and energy for construction are relatively poor, sometimes the only available were from non-realised projects (in USA and DE). The THORP plant (BNFL, Sellafield, UK) and its adjoint facilities (for vitrification and conditioning of waste from light water reactors) have been used as main reference for the estimation of the infrastructure, although for the operation most of the data are for UP2 and UP3 plants (Cogema, La Hague, FR). Annual design throughput is 1200 tonne heavy metal. Extrapolations have been made to take into account visual estimations and aerial photos of the facilities. No direct emissions during construction are considered, only indirect through the energy (and material) requirements. Decommissioning is only very roughly described. Only non-radioactive wastes from dismantling are accounded for, because low radioactive wastes are attributed to operation.;
UUID: 1582dc6e-e029-3b4e-9c8e-1c0ab1a0053e</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
